---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Privacy Policy | MD Toolkit"
  description="MD Toolkit processes every conversion locally in your browser. Nothing is uploaded to a server."
>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="tool-head">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Short version: your documents never leave your device.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>Do you upload my files?</summary>
          <p>
            No. Every conversion runs in your browser with JavaScript. Content you paste or drop into
            the editor is processed on your device and is never sent to a server.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is stored locally?</summary>
          <p>
            The editor keeps a draft in <code>localStorage</code> so a reload does not lose your work.
            Clearing site data removes it.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Third-party scripts</summary>
          <p>
            Production deployments typically add analytics and advertising scripts. If you enable
            them, disclose them here and in the cookie banner — this is also what AdSense requires.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .tool-head { padding: 36px 0 4px; max-width: 760px; }
  .tool-head h1 { font-size: clamp(24px, 3.2vw, 34px); margin: 0 0 10px; font-weight: 600; }
  .tool-head p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-soft); }
</style>
